      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add an eval/unit case: an unbacked free-string suggestion does NOT render (guards FR-04 / task 021).</step>
    <step order="2">Add a case: "prioritize my tasks" maps to the FR-01 advisory capability and works, or is absent (guards FR-04).</step>
    <step order="3">Add cases: the Daily Briefing / Smart To Do follow-on cards are gated on the tab's open state — suppressed when open, shown + launching the correct surface when closed (guards FR-06 / task 023).</step>
    <step order="4">Confirm each case passes on current behavior and fails when the guarded behavior is regressed (reintroduced dead-end / ungated card).</step>
    <step order="5">/conflict-check before the PR; update TASK-INDEX ✅.</step>
  </steps>
  <justification>
    <existing>The ADR-039 golden-utterance suite + the task-021/023 test suites exist; no E2 dead-end / card-gating coverage exists yet.</existing>
    <extension>Add cases to the existing suites — no new test harness.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-04 / FR-06 can regress silently: a dead-end suggestion or an ungated (duplicate-tab) card could reappear with no failing test.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <outputs>
    <output type="test">FR-04 eval/unit cases (unbacked suggestion suppressed; "prioritize my tasks" works or absent)</output>
    <output type="test">FR-06 eval/unit cases (Briefing / Smart To Do cards gated on tab open state)</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The FR-04 cases are added and pass (unbacked suggestion does not render; "prioritize my tasks" works or is absent).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The FR-06 cases are added and pass (Briefing / Smart To Do cards suppressed when the tab is open, shown when closed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A reintroduced dead-end suggestion fails the FR-04 case (negative).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An ungated card (that would open a duplicate tab) fails the FR-06 case (negative).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Deps 021 + 023 must land first (behavior to cover). Cover both FR-04 and FR-06 with genuine negative regression guards per ADR-038 (no scaffolding/DI/ctor-null tests). Add "prioritize my tasks" to the ADR-039 golden-utterance suite as an FR-01-backed case. /conflict-check before the PR.

  ── COMPLETION (2026-08-17, sonnet/high FULL, TEST-MODIFYING) ──
  KEY FINDING: the FR-04/FR-06 regression guards were ALREADY authored WITH their features (the ADR-038-preferred pattern — tests land in the feature PR, not a separate task): 021a `AssistantSuggestionServiceTests` (service off-catalog drop / typed kinds / cadence / scope), 021b SprkChat suggestion suites (client untyped/unbacked drop, typed render), 023 `agendaFollowOnCards.test.tsx` (FR-06 card open-tab gating — suppressed-when-open negatives), and 013 golden case AR4-003 ("help me prioritize my tasks" → real list-tasks capability). Per ADR-038's BINDING anti-scaffolding rule + §11, duplicating these would be build-class waste (deleted at /test-diet).

  DELIVERED (the one guard the golden-utterance gate genuinely owed + the auditable FR-10 map):
  (1) `AssistantEnhancementsR4EvalTests.cs` — NEW fact `SuggestFollowupsAction_IsGroundedTypedTwoKindProposer_NoDeadEndFreeString` (FR-04 no-dead-end CONTRACT anchor): grounds the `suggest-followups` Action as a closed-candidate, typed two-kind {capability|question} proposer with the verbatim-copy + drop-off-catalog prompt rules — a revert to the retired ungrounded free-string generator fails it. The catalog/prompt-contract analog of the E1 `ListTasksAction_Declares...` fact; distinct from 021a's service-logic test. Joins the `Category=GoldenUtteranceEval` merge gate. **8/8 R4 eval tests pass** (dotnet test, net10). Build 0 errors.
  (2) `tests/integration/contract/Eval/README.md` — refreshed the stale "SCAFFOLDED, no harness" section (013 built it) + added the "E2 (task 024) FR-04 / FR-06 coverage map" table mapping each acceptance criterion → its guarding test + the negative-guard property, and documenting that FR-06 is pure client UX (no golden-utterance-gate home by design).
  (3) `behavior-gap-register.md` — P2 row Status → ✅ with the FR-10 guard citation + an E2 coverage-map note + the deferred residual.
  (4) `notes/defer-issues.md` — D-024-01 (endpoint typed-`suggestions` guard): initially deferred; **fixed in-project** on owner steer (2026-08-17: don't defer without a better owner). The inline emit block was extracted to the testable `ChatEndpoints.BuildTypedFollowups` (behavior-preserving) + guarded by `ChatEndpointsTypedFollowupsTests` (order action→capability→question, null-binding-capability dropped, empty⇒no event) via InternalsVisibleTo. Full BFF suite green; no new packages/CVEs; publish size unchanged (pure refactor). This closes the typed-shape guard end-to-end (Action-contract fact + service 021a + client-parse 021b + endpoint guard).

  ACCEPTANCE: all 4 criteria met — FR-04 cases present+pass (AR4-003 + new fact), FR-06 present+pass (023), reintroduced dead-end fails FR-04 (new fact + 021a drop), ungated card fails FR-06 (023). Step 9.5: code-review (maintain-class KEEP-path fact, no B1–B17 antipattern) + adr-check (ADR-038/039) PASS. No BFF source touched (test + docs only) — no publish/CVE impact.
